#. ~ Description for closed reinforced glass door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A closed glass door reinforced with woven steel wires in a stylish, but "
"practical pattern."
msgstr ""
"Zamknięte drzwi ze zbrojonego szkła, z wtopionymi stylowo, aczkolwiek "
"praktycznie metalowymi drutami."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open reinforced glass door"
msgstr "otwarte drzwi ze zbrojonego szkła"

#. ~ Description for open reinforced glass door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A glass door reinforced with woven steel wires in a stylish, but practical "
"pattern.  Yep, it's open."
msgstr ""
"Drzwi ze zbrojonego szkła, z wtopionymi stylowo, aczkolwiek praktycznie "
"metalowymi drutami. Tak, otwarte."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed wood door"
msgstr "zamknięte drewniane drzwi"

#. ~ Description for closed wood door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn"
" easily, too."
msgstr ""
"Standardowe drewniane drzwi, które nie wyglądają na zbyt wytrzymałe. "
"Prawdopodobnie łatwo się też palą."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open wood door"
msgstr "otwarte drewniane drzwi"

#. ~ Description for open wood door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn"
" easily, too.  This one is wide open."
msgstr ""
"Standardowe drewniane drzwi, które nie wyglądają na zbyt wytrzymałe. "
"Prawdopodobnie łatwo się też palą. Te są otwarte na oścież."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "damaged wood door"
msgstr "uszkodzone drewniane drzwi"

#. ~ Description for damaged wood door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A trashed wooden door, that is more of an obstacle than a door.  Also, you "
"can see right through it.  It could be boarded up with a few two by fours."
msgstr ""
"Zniszczone drewniane drzwi, bardziej przeszkoda niż drzwi. Możesz widzieć "
"przez nie na wylot. Można je zabić kilkoma deskami."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "empty door frame"
msgstr "pusta futryna"

#. ~ Description for empty door frame
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An empty door frame made from two by fours and nails.  A variety of doors "
"could be constructed here."
msgstr ""
"Pusta ościeżnica z dwóch desek i gwoździ. Można tu zamontować różne rodzaje "
"drzwi."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed glass door"
msgstr "zamknięte szklane drzwi"

#. ~ Description for closed glass door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A sliding glass door, the kind that was on social media with people and "
"animals running into.  This one is closed, so don't hurt yourself."
msgstr ""
"Przesuwne szklane drzwi, często pokazywane w social media jako obiekty, na "
"które wpadali ludzie i zwierzęta. Te są zamknięte więc nie zrób sobie "
"krzywdy."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open glass door"
msgstr "otwarte szklane drzwi"

#. ~ Description for open glass door
#. ~ Description for open frosted glass door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A sliding glass door that has been left open for all manner of things to "
"travel through."
msgstr "Przesuwne szklane drzwi otwarte na wszelki przechodzący ruch."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed wood door with peephole"
msgstr "zamknięte drewniane drzwi z judaszem"

#. ~ Description for closed wood door with peephole
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A regular door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  If "
"you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole."
msgstr ""
"Zwykłe drewniane drzwi, z tym że te mają wizjer. Jeśli je zbadasz dokładnie,"
" możesz zerknąć przez dziurkę."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "damaged wood door with peephole"
msgstr "uszkodzone drewniane drzwi z judaszem"

#. ~ Description for damaged wood door with peephole
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Bad news is the peephole is broken and you can't look outside the door.  "
"Good news is the door is nearly broken down, so there's nothing blocking the"
" view.  A few planks, nails and the right tools could patch up all the "
"damage."
msgstr ""
"Zła nowina to to że wizjer jest zniszczony, a dobra to że drzwi także więc i"
" tak wszystko widać na przestrzał. Kilka desek, gwoździ i odpowiednie "
"narzędzia załatałyby wszelkie uszkodzenia."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open wood door with peephole"
msgstr "otwarte drewniane drzwi z judaszem"

#. ~ Description for open wood door with peephole
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A regular door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  If "
"you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole.  "
"Although, you don't need to peek through it since the door is open anyway."
msgstr ""
"Zwykłe drewniane drzwi, z tym że te mają wizjer. Jeśli je zbadasz dokładnie,"
" możesz zerknąć przez dziurkę. Z tym że nie ma potrzeby bo są otwarte na "
"oścież."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed reinforced wood door"
msgstr "zamknięte wzmocnione drewniane drzwi"

#. ~ Description for closed reinforced wood door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Just like other wooden doors, except this one has layers of nailed in two by"
" fours and additional hinge for reinforcement.  It might be barricaded, but "
"still susceptible to fire."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "damaged reinforced wood door"
msgstr "uszkodzone wzmocnione drewniane drzwi"

#. ~ Description for damaged reinforced wood door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"There are splintering planks and visible holes in the wood, it looks like it"
" could be smashed apart if not repaired."
msgstr ""
"Są to rozszczepione deski i dziury w drewnie, więc wygląda na to, że można "
"to rozwalić jeśli nie zostanie naprawione."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open reinforced wood door"
msgstr "otwarte wzmocnione drewniane drzwi"

#. ~ Description for open reinforced wood door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Just like other wooden doors, except this one has layers of nailed in two by"
" fours for reinforcement.  It might be fortified, but still susceptible to "
"fire.  It's open so it's not stopping anything right now."
msgstr ""
"Wyglądają jak inne drewniane drzwi, ale pokryte są warstwami przybitych doń "
"desek jako wzmocnienie. Mogą być zabarykadowane, ale nadal nie oprą się "
"ogniowi. Są otwarte, wiec niczego nie zatrzymują."

#. ~ Description for closed wood door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn"
" easily, too.  This one has an extra keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You "
"could pry it open or pick the lock."
msgstr ""
"Standardowe drewniane drzwi, które nie wyglądają na zbyt wytrzymałe. "
"Prawdopodobnie łatwo się też palą. Te zaopatrzono w zamek więc pewnie są "
"zamknięte na klucz. Możesz je wyważyć lub spróbować otworzyć zamek "
"wytrychem."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "You pry open the door."
msgstr "Wyważasz drzwi na oścież."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "You pry, but cannot pry open the door."
msgstr "Próbujesz wyważać, ale nie możesz wyważyć drzwi."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "You damage the door!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "With a satisfying click, the lock on the door opens."
msgstr "Z satysfakcjonującym kliknięciem, zamek w drzwiach otwiera się."

#. ~ Description for closed wood door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn"
" easily, too.  This one has a deadbolt keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You "
"could pry it open or pick the lock, or unlock the deadbolt from the inside."
msgstr ""
"Standardowe drewniane drzwi, które nie wyglądają na zbyt wytrzymałe. "
"Prawdopodobnie łatwo się też palą. Te zaopatrzono w zasuwkę, więc pewnie są "
"zamknięte. Możesz je wyważyć, spróbować otworzyć wytrychem lub odryglować od"
" środka."

#. ~ Description for closed wood door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A regular door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  If "
"you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole.  This "
"one has a deadbolt keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You could pry it open or"
" pick the lock, or unlock the deadbolt from the inside."
msgstr ""
"Zwykłe drewniane drzwi, z tym że te mają wizjer. Jeśli je zbadasz dokładnie,"
" możesz zerknąć przez dziurkę. Te zaopatrzono w zasuwkę, więc pewnie są "
"zamknięte. Możesz je wyważyć, spróbować otworzyć wytrychem lub odryglować od"
" środka."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed door curtain"
msgstr "zasłonięta kurtyna na drzwi"

#. ~ Description for closed door curtain
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Repurposed curtains from a window acting as a door.  Could be easily taken "
"down for supplies or placed somewhere else."
msgstr ""
"Zasłona okienna przerobiona na drzwi. Łatwo ją zdjąć by użyć gdzie indziej "
"lub przerobić na materiały."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed makeshift door"
msgstr "zamknięte prowizoryczne drzwi"

#. ~ Description for closed makeshift door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A makeshift screen consisting of two by fours bound together with vertical "
"rope hanging from the top of the doorway.  Could be easily taken down and "
"re-purposed."
msgstr ""
"Prowizoryczna zasłona z dwóch desek powiązanych pionowo liną zwisającą z "
"ościeżnicy. Łatwo rozebrać i wykorzystać do innych celów."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "wham."
msgstr "wham."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open door curtain"
msgstr "odsłonięta kurtyna na drzwi"

#. ~ Description for open door curtain
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Repurposed curtains from a window acting as a door.  Could be easily taken "
"down for supplies or placed somewhere else.  These curtains are open, "
"bundled and tied next to the doorway."
msgstr ""
"Zasłona okienna przerobiona na drzwi. Łatwo ją zdjąć by użyć gdzie indziej "
"lub przerobić na materiały. Drzwi są otwarte, a zasłonę zwinięto i "
"przywiązano do ościeżnicy."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open makeshift door"
msgstr "otwarte prowizoryczne drzwi"

#. ~ Description for open makeshift door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A makeshift screen consisting of two by fours bound together with rope "
"hanging from the top of the doorway.  Could be easily taken down and re-"
"purposed.  The planks have been rolled up and attached to the top of the "
"doorway, allowing free movement through."
msgstr ""
"Prowizoryczna zasłona z dwóch desek powiązanych pionowo liną zwisającą z "
"ościeżnicy. Łatwo rozebrać i wykorzystać do innych celów. Deski zwinięto i "
"przywiązano do ościeżnicy, zapewniając swobodne przejście."

#. ~ Description for empty door frame
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An empty door frame made from wood.  A variety of doors could be constructed"
" here."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "empty metal door frame"
msgstr "pusta metalowa futryna"

#. ~ Description for empty metal door frame
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An empty door frame made of steel and assorted metal.  A variety of doors "
"could be constructed here."
msgstr ""
"Pusta ościeżnica ze stali i innych metali. Można tu zamontować różne rodzaje"
" drzwi."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "empty metal window frame"
msgstr "pusta metalowa rama okienna"

#. ~ Description for empty metal window frame
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An empty window frame constructed from assembled metal and carefully braced "
"with various hardware."
msgstr "Pusta futryna z metalu ostrożnie osadzona z pomocą narzędzi."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "boarded up door"
msgstr "zabite deskami drzwi"

#. ~ Description for boarded up door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that has several planks across it, nailed down to "
"board it up and increase its durability.  Still flammable though."
msgstr ""
"Standardowe drewniane drzwi z kilkoma przybitymi deskami dla wzmocnienia "
"konstrukcji i zwiększenia odporności. Nadal łatwopalne."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "boarded up damaged door"
msgstr "zabite deskami uszkodzone drzwi"

#. ~ Description for boarded up damaged door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A boarded up wooden door, except some of the planks are fractured or coming "
"loose.  Without repairs, it could be broken down easily."
msgstr ""
"Zabite deskami drzwi, z tym że niektóre deski odpadły, a inne popękały. Bez "
"naprawy będzie je można łatwo sforsować."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "boarded up door with peephole"
msgstr "zabite deskami drzwi z judaszem"

#. ~ Description for boarded up door with peephole
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A boarded up door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  "
"Although it's been covered up in planks, you could still examine the "
"peephole."
msgstr ""
"Zabite deskami zwykłe drewniane drzwi, z tym że te mają wizjer. Mimo że "
"wzmocnione drewnem, nadal możesz zbadać je by zerknąć na zewnątrz przez "
"otwór."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "boarded up reinforced door"
msgstr "zabite deskami wzmocnione drzwi"

#. ~ Description for boarded up reinforced door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An additionally reinforced door of layered two by fours that has been "
"boarded up with more wood to prevent it from opening.  Still susceptible to "
"fire."
msgstr ""
"Wzmocnione warstwami desek drzwi zabito na amen kolejnymi deskami, żeby "
"uniemożliwić ich otwarcie. Nadal wrażliwe na ogień."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "boarded up damaged reinforced door"
msgstr "zabite deskami uszkodzone wzmocnione drzwi"

#. ~ Description for boarded up damaged reinforced door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A battered and torn reinforced door with planks bursting from the joints.  "
"The boarded up two by fours are fragmented and in pieces, this doesn't look "
"like an easy repair."
msgstr ""
"Rozbite i rozerwane wzmocnione drzwi z deskami sterczącymi z zawiasów. "
"Wzmacniające je deski są popękane i w kawałkach, co nie wygląda na łatwą "
"naprawę."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "boarded up damaged door with peephole"
msgstr "zabite deskami uszkodzone drzwi z judaszem"

#. ~ Description for boarded up damaged door with peephole
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A wrecked door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  "
"Although it's been covered up in planks, the peephole was damaged and can't "
"be used to see through."
msgstr ""
"Zrujnowane drewniane drzwi, z tym że te mają wizjer. Wizjer jest rozbity "
"więc nie można przez niego zerkać."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed metal door"
msgstr "zamknięte metalowe drzwi"

#. ~ Description for closed metal door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape."
msgstr ""
"Niezwykle wytrzymałe drzwi zrobione ze stalowych elementów dociętych i "
"zbitych ze sobą na wymiar."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "metal wall"
msgstr "metalowa ściana"

#. ~ Description for metal wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"An industrially fabricated thick sheet carefully positioned and joined "
"seamlessly with perimeter sealant, this wall is capable of resisting extreme"
" elements as well as hostile forces.  Blast load rated and extremely fire-"
"retardant, breaching will require specialized tools or industrial vehicles."
msgstr ""
"Fabrycznie stworzona gruba płyta dokładnie ułożona i połączona jednolicie na"
" brzegach szczeliwem. Ściana z wielkiej płyty jest zdolna wytrzymać "
"ekstremalne warunki jak i agresywne siły. Mierzona pod względem odporności "
"na ładunki wybuchowe i niezwykle ognioodporna, będzie wymagać "
"wyspecjalizowanych narzędzi lub pojazdów przemysłowych do jej sforsowania."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open secret door"
msgstr "otwarte sekretne drzwi"

#. ~ Description for open secret door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"This apparently normal segment of metal wall has opened to reveal a secret "
"passage."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open metal door"
msgstr "otwarte metalowe drzwi"

#. ~ Description for open metal door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  It's open, so no tools are needed to break in."
msgstr ""
"Niezwykle wytrzymałe drzwi zrobione ze stalowych elementów dociętych i "
"zbitych ze sobą na wymiar. Są otwarte, wiec nie potrzeba narzędzi by się "
"włamywać."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed metal door with peephole"
msgstr "zamknięte metalowe drzwi z judaszem"

#. ~ Description for closed metal door with peephole
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  If you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the "
"hole."
msgstr ""
"Niezwykle wytrzymałe drzwi zrobione ze stalowych elementów dociętych i "
"zbitych ze sobą na wymiar. Po dokładnym zbadaniu możesz zerknąć przez "
"wizjer."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open metal door with peephole"
msgstr "otwarte metalowe drzwi z judaszem"

#. ~ Description for open metal door with peephole
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  If you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the "
"hole.  Although, you don't need to peek through it since the door is open "
"anyway."
msgstr ""
"Niezwykle wytrzymałe drzwi zrobione ze stalowych elementów dociętych i "
"zbitych ze sobą na wymiar. Po dokładnym zbadaniu możesz zerknąć przez "
"wizjer. Ale nie ma po co bo są otwarte."

#. ~ Description for closed metal door
#. ~ Description for underwater closed metal door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A galvanized steel door, forged to withstand punishment and impede anyone or"
" anything.  Typically used in conjunction with automated electronic locking "
"mechanisms that require an external source to unlock."
msgstr ""
"Galwanizowane stalowe drzwi, wykute by wytrzymać atak i zatrzymać "
"kogokolwiek i cokolwiek. Zwykle używane w połączeniu z automatycznymi "
"elektronicznymi zamkami wymagającymi zewnętrznych elementów odmykających."

#. ~ Description for open metal door
#. ~ Description for underwater open metal door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A hanging metal gate.  Typically used in conjunction with mechanical winch."
"  Probably shouldn't be underneath when it comes down."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "underwater closed metal door"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "underwater open metal door"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for closed metal door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  This one has an extra keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You could "
"probably pick the lock, or a very strong tool could pry it open."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed junk metal door"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for closed junk metal door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A makeshift door made of rusty scrap metal bolted together, with metal wires"
" for hinges.  Very fashionable in post-apocalyptic shantytowns."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open junk metal door"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for open junk metal door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A makeshift door made of rusty scrap metal bolted together, with metal wires"
" for hinges.  Very fashionable in post-apocalyptic shantytowns.  Somehow "
"even draftier now that it's open."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed bar door"
msgstr "zamknięte drzwi z krat"

#. ~ Description for closed bar door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A detention door made up of crisscrossed stainless steel bars.  The locking "
"mechanism doesn't appear to be engaged."
msgstr ""
"Drzwi celi zrobione z krzyżujących się nierdzewnych stalowych prętów. "
"Mechanizm ryglujący nie wydaje się być uruchomiony."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open bar door"
msgstr "otwarte drzwi z krat"

#. ~ Description for open bar door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A detention door made up of crisscrossed stainless steel bars.  It's swung "
"wide open.  Freedom!"
msgstr ""
"Drzwi celi zrobione z krzyżujących się nierdzewnych stalowych prętów. Są "
"szeroko otwarte. Wolność!"

#. ~ Description for closed bar door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A detention door made up of crisscrossed stainless steel bars.  The locking "
"mechanism appears to be engaged.  The mechanism could be picked open with "
"enough skill."
msgstr ""
"Drzwi celi zrobione z krzyżujących się nierdzewnych stalowych prętów. "
"Mechanizm ryglujący wydaje się być uruchomiony. Mechanizm ten można by "
"złamać wytrychem mając odrobinę umiejętności."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "The door swings open…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed frosted glass door"
msgstr "zamknięte drzwi z matowego szkła"

#. ~ Description for closed frosted glass door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A sliding door of frosted white glass."
msgstr "Przesuwne drzwi z matowego białego szkła."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open frosted glass door"
msgstr "otwarte drzwi z matowego szkła"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed bulkhead door"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for closed bulkhead door
#. ~ Description for open bulkhead door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door of cast metal, it is watertight and opened using"
" the fly wheel."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open bulkhead door"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "underwater closed bulkhead door"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for underwater closed bulkhead door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door of cast metal, opened using the fly wheel.  It's"
" technically still watertight, but that's a moot point when both sides are "
"flooded."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "underwater open bulkhead door"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for underwater open bulkhead door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door of cast metal, currently open and letting all "
"the fish in."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "welded metal door"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for welded metal door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  It's been welded shut, that oughta hold 'em."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "welded metal door with peephole"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for welded metal door with peephole
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  It's been welded shut, that oughta hold 'em.  If you examined it "
"more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "welded bulkhead door"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for welded bulkhead door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient watertight door of cast metal.  Used to open using "
"the fly wheel, it's since been welded shut.  That oughta hold 'em."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "welded bar door"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for welded bar door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A detention door made up of crisscrossed stainless steel bars.  It's been "
"welded shut, that oughta hold 'em."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed screen door"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for closed screen door
#. ~ Description for open screen door
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A simple wooden doorway with screen mesh."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "rattle!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open screen door"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "palisade gate"
msgstr "brama palisady"

#. ~ Description for palisade gate
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A large doorway consisting of long logs cabled together, that could be "
"expanded upon.  Can act as a door if some type of pulley system were rigged "
"on an adjacent palisade wall."
msgstr ""
"Duża brama z długich drewnianych pali powiązanych ze sobą, którą można "
"poszerzyć. Może działać jak drzwi jeżeli do sąsiedniej palisady przymocować "
"system lin i bloczków."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "open palisade gate"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for open palisade gate
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A hanging palisade gate, hoisted by a nearby pulley system.  Probably "
"shouldn't be underneath when it comes down."
msgstr ""
"Wisząca brama palisadowa, utrzymywana przez pobliski system lin i bloczków. "
"Prawdopodobnie wolałbyś nie stać pod nią gdy zostanie opuszczona w dół."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "makeshift portcullis"
msgstr "prowizoryczna brona"

#. ~ Description for makeshift portcullis
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"An immense gateway scrapped together with various bits of steel and metal "
"scraps."
msgstr ""
"Wielka brama zbita z różnych kawałków stali i innych metalowych kawałków "
"złomu."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "locked wire gate"
msgstr "zamknięta na klucz brama druciana"

#. ~ Description for locked wire gate
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A gate for a chain link fence.  This one has a locked padlock on the latch "
"system.  With the right tools, you could cut the metal fence, pick the lock,"
" or pry the whole thing open.  You could also examine the fence to see if it"
" looks climbable."
msgstr ""

#. ~ sound of bolt cutting locked wire gate
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "Gachunk!"
msgstr "Gachunk!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "You pry open the gate."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "You pry, but cannot pry open the gate."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "With a satisfying click, the lock on the gate opens."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "closed wire gate"
msgstr "otwarta brama druciana"

#. ~ Description for closed wire gate
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A gate for a chain link fence with a latch system to stay closed."
msgstr "Brama do siatki drucianej z zatrzaskiem by być zamkniętym."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "open wire gate"
msgstr "otwarta brama druciana"

#. ~ Description for open wire gate
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A gate for a chain link fence with a latch system to stay closed.  The latch"
" is undone, so the gate has swung open."
msgstr ""
"Brama do siatki drucianej z zatrzaskiem by być zamkniętym. Zatrzask jest "
"otwarty a brama stoi otworem."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "closed wooden gate"
msgstr "zamknięta drewniana brama"

